; continuous), gender (male, female), residence (metropolitan, suburb or rural), education (none, primary, secondary, tertiary), smoking (never/ever), medication use of chloromycetin (no/yes), occupational exposure to benzene (no/yes), and organophosphorus (no/yes).</p></fn><fn id="t3-fn3"><label>b</label><p>Two-sided test for trend across quantitative or ordinal quantitative variables.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>